 "pages": [
  {
   "number": 1,
   "text": "01 / MEMORY & LEARNING\nRetrieval practice\nRetrieval practice means trying to recall information from memory.\nA retrieval attempt happens before looking at the answer.\nChecking the answer gives feedback after the attempt.\nSYNTHETIC EXAMPLE / prepared for application testing",
   "width": 1500,
   "height": 844,
   "warning": ""
  },
  {
   "number": 2,
   "text": "02 / MEMORY & LEARNING\nSpace your practice\nSpaced practice distributes study sessions over time.\nMassed practice groups study into one continuous session.\nA review schedule decides when a card should be studied again.\nSYNTHETIC EXAMPLE / prepared for application testing",
   "width": 1500,
   "height": 844,
   "warning": ""
  },
  {
   "number": 3,
   "text": "03 / MEMORY & LEARNING\nMake a useful card\nAn atomic card tests one clear idea.\nA source reference points back to the supporting lecture page.\nAn ambiguous question can have more than one plausible answer.\nSYNTHETIC EXAMPLE / prepared for application testing",
   "width": 1500,
   "height": 844,
   "warning": ""
  },
  {
   "number": 4,
   "text": "",
   "width": 1500,
